message: "If you use this repository, please cite it as below."
title: "Passing the prop-firm challenge: rules, calibrated return processes, skill inference and the economics of evaluation fees"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23537728
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Solano Paul"
    given-names: "Sean"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-8465-4468"
    affiliation: "Independent researcher"
license: MIT
version: "2.1"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
abstract: "Code, rule dataset, simulation results, figures and analysis plan for a study of retail proprietary-trading evaluations (challenges). Version 2 covers the public rules of 17 products at 12 firms (read 13 October to 17 November 2026): how often a trader with zero skill passes (median 20.4% across 409 resolved settings), which rules drive failure, how much a pass reveals about skill (likelihood ratio about 2 to 3.4 at a 56% hit rate), and what the rules imply for firm revenue. The October study of ten products at eight firms is kept in the repository root. Archived firm-page text and market data are not redistributed."
keywords:
  - "proprietary trading"
